Z||000000||Avery Montembeault||10-01-2001||09:27 PM||||I belive it has come time to replace my clutch. I can hear it slipping and it has 88k on it. i was wondering what the best economical clutch kit out there is, from peoples experience. sorry, I just cant dump the money into a $300 kevlar clutch. Do I need to drop the engine, or is it possible to change the clutch through the wheel well?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Jefrysuko||10-01-2001||10:13 PM||||Yes it is possible to change the clutch without dropping the cradle.  I am one of the poor souls who used this method and I will never do it that way again.  I thought that I would save time and money by not dropping the cradle but that wasn't the case.  As for a clutch I have heard Borg-Warner is the stock replacement and I have used them in other cars with satifaction.  Centerforce is also popular and not that much more expensive and from what I have experienced is very smooth operating.  Good Luck and have fun.<BR>Jeffrey<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif"> ||||reg||1
